In article <2505@wheaton.UUCP> water@wheaton.UUCP (Paul Waterman) writes:
>I've still got a page of one liners on things that we're working on
>adding to the spoiler file.  Some of those one liners could produce several
>k of spoilers each.  Also, we're working on implementing an unofficial patch
>to nethack to allow nethackers to directly access the spoilers from within
>the game, as well as better monster descriptions, and many other things, so
>don't worry - there will be more spoilers.
>
>          - Paul

First off, my great thanks to Paul Waterman and co. for taking the
awesome amount of time that must have gone into creating the spoiler
file. For those of us who always hit <space> when prompted by the
**SPOILERS AHEAD** ^L in rec.games.hack, it really helps us learn
almost everything that there is to know about the game.

The only problem is that (like nethack itself) each new revision keeps
on getting larger and larger. The problem is that the spoilers have
alienated themselves somewhat from general players, i.e. those who
just want to learn a little bit about the game and figure out how to
survive past level 6, because they are too overwhelmed by the vastness
of the spoiler's size and the overwhelming amount of detail. Version
5.35 is more than 250K, 4200 lines, and 70 pages!

In the current spoiler file, we have the complete listings of each
monster and how much food nutrition that you get from it, as well as
the complete formulas (several pages) for how much damage a weapon
does, etc. Although there is a section on frequently asked questions
(one of the best sections, IMO), I would suggest that what we are
starting to need now is a spoiler file for the spoiler file. I've had
friends who have read the entire spoiler file, but then proceed to
lose their best game after killing a cockatrice because they didn't
have any gloves. There's no obvious area in the spoiler file (there
is, but I can't find it, and by the time one gets done with it they
may have forgotten it) that says some of the general things you should
do to avoid dying (in unexpected ways).

Perhaps one addition that could be made is adding a section on general
hints that one should have memorized and to keep in mind while
playing, which aren't really spoilers, but are about the more
dangerous things in the dungeons, e.g. a) Don't hit a floating eye
unless blind. b) watch out for mumakils - they're really dangerous. c)
watch out for ochre jellys for the same reason. d) watch for trolls
when low on hp - they will come back to life after a few turns, etc.
We could also have a list of ways one can suddenly die, and what one
can do to prevent them. For instance, I have the following list:

Ways to suddenly die (there may be a few others, but these are the main ones):
	1) Eating a rotted corpse
	2) Choking on food
	3) Falling in water
	4) When a cockatrice gets a good hit on you
	5) Touching a cockatrice corpse
	6) Looking upon medusa
	7) From the "touch of death" from the Wizard or other nasties
	8) Entering hell without fire resistance
	9) From fighting a gremlin when it removes an important intrinsic
	   (e.g. your fire resistance in hell)

Either way, I think the spoiler file is a very valuable asset and has
helped me out of many a close call. It can use a few
changes/additions, but although "More is better" may be true in the
dungeon for Wraiths, it's definitely not true for Black Puddings :-)

